const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"研究问题",en:"Research question"},body:{zh:"论文考察社交媒体文章和读者评论中的投资者观点，是否预测未来股票收益和盈余意外。 阅读时应把它理解为受样本、时点和制度限定的问题，而不是可以脱离条件的结论。",en:"The article investigates whether investor opinions in social-media articles and their reader commentaries predict future stock returns and earnings surprises. Read it as a bounded question, not as a conclusion that automatically travels beyond its sample, dates, or institutional setting."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/hhu001",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (2014) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (2014) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"研究设计",en:"Research design"},body:{zh:"它对美国投资者社交媒体平台进行文本分析，并分别考察作者文章和回应评论。 比较对象、观察窗口和对照关系共同构成研究合同；改变其中一项，可能改变所检验的命题。",en:"It applies textual analysis to a U.S. investor social-media platform and separately considers author articles and response commentaries. The comparison, observation window, and control relation are part of the research contract; changing one can change the proposition being tested."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/hhu001",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (2014) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (2014) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"数据与时点",en:"Data and timing"},body:{zh:"输入包括获许可且版本化的文章和评论文本、作者与公司映射、首次可见时点、文本处理规则、收益、盈余意外定义和覆盖过滤。 字段定义、可得时点和样本筛选需要与原研究分别记录，不能仅因变量同名或使用最新修订值就视为可比。",en:"Inputs include permitted, versioned article and comment text, author and firm mappings, first-visible timestamps, text-processing rules, returns, earnings-surprise definitions, and coverage filters. Keep fields, availability timing, and sample filters separate from the original study: a same-named variable or later-revised database is not automatically comparable."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/hhu001",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (2014) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (2014) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"如何理解结果",en:"How to read the result"},body:{zh:"摘要报告平台样本中的预测模式，不验证每条帖子、不表示群体观点为真，也不提供实时预测服务。 它只支持来源所描述的经验或理论关系，不能把相关性、模型拟合或历史表现升级为因果、可执行性或未来保证。",en:"The abstract reports predictive patterns in its platform sample; it does not validate every post, imply that crowd opinion is true, or provide a live forecasting service. This remains the empirical or theoretical relation described by the source; it does not turn association, fit, or historical performance into causality, an executable procedure, or a future guarantee."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/hhu001",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (2014) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (2014) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"复核清单",en:"Replication checks"},body:{zh:"记录采集权利和版本历史；去重编辑或转载内容；区分发布与采集时点；将标签和验证样本排除在训练外。 开展后续分析前，应将这些选择写入版本化研究记录，并保留原始来源链接与访问日期。",en:"Record collection rights and version history; deduplicate edited or reposted content; separate publication from ingestion time; keep labels and validation samples out of training. Before extending the analysis, record these choices in a versioned note and retain the primary-source link and access date."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/hhu001",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (2014) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (2014) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"适用边界",en:"Scope boundary"},body:{zh:"该条导读引用 Review of Financial Studies (2014)。平台构成、审核、幸存、语言和选择性会改变结果；该导读不授予数据权利或交易建议。 如需数值结论、参数、表格或稳健性检验，请回到原文并单独核对版本、附录与样本定义。",en:"This guide cites Review of Financial Studies (2014). Platform composition, moderation, survivorship, language, and selection can alter results, so this guide grants neither data rights nor a trading recommendation. For numerical conclusions, parameters, tables, or robustness tests, return to the original and separately verify the edition, appendices, and sample definitions."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/hhu001",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (2014) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (2014) · source description"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"本文只整理“Wisdom of Crowds: The Value of Stock Opinions Transmitted Through Social Media”公开说明的研究对象与设计边界，不构成收益预测、交易规则或全文复现。平台构成、审核、幸存、语言和选择性会改变结果；该导读不授予数据权利或交易建议。",en:"This guide only organizes the publicly described question and design of “Wisdom of Crowds: The Value of Stock Opinions Transmitted Through Social Media”. It is not a return forecast, trading rule, or full-text replication. The source's stated scope remains controlling."}};export{e as default};
